(lang dune 3.10)

; This example is a subproject isolated from the top-level tola build.
;
; Why: `canary/examples/tiny/ocaml/dune` uses `(c_library_flags -ltiny)`
; which requires LIBRARY_PATH pointing at c/build/. Top-level `dune build`
; at the tola root cannot satisfy that without env setup, and would
; sometimes leave the shared `_build/` in a stale wrap-vs-nowrap state
; (interference with canary scenario direct-compiles). Making this a
; nested project confines its `_build/` and stops top-level recursion.
;
; Canonical entry: `make -C canary/examples/tiny/ ocaml` (sets
; LIBRARY_PATH + LD_RUN_PATH before invoking dune). Direct
; `dune build` from this dir works if LIBRARY_PATH is set.
